      "scope": "Launch date",
      "claim": "The Small Astronomy Satellite (Uhuru) was launched on December 12, 1970.",
      "answer": "December 12, 1970",
      "quote": "It was also known as the X-ray Explorer Satellite, SAS-A (for \"Small Astronomy Satellite\" A, being first of the three-spacecraft SAS series), SAS 1, or Explorer 42. The observatory was launched on December 12, 1970 into an initial orbit of about 560 km apogee, 520 km perigee, 3 degrees inclination, with a period of 96 minutes.",
